1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
For iPhone users, two brilliant
features - let me show you.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,600
Useful for a lot of people.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,000
It's not new - it's an old feature,

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,680
but far more people don't know it than do,

5
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,600
so I made this video.

6
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:14,170
If you already know it,

7
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:16,240
share this video with those who don't -

8
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,790
let everyone know this is possible.

9
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,470
If you like it, hit like

10
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,450
and drop your thoughts in the comments.

11
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,820
So, what are the tips?

12
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,620
Tip one: taking screenshots.

13
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:28,890
Normally, we take a screenshot

14
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:31,770
by pressing two buttons
- power and volume down -

15
00:00:31,770 --> 00:00:33,600
at the same time,

16
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:37,200
or by adding a shortcut to take one.

17
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:40,900
There's something simpler,
built into the iPhone.

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,700
Many may know it, but more people don't,

19
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,100
so here's the video.

20
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,310
So how do we do it?

21
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:51,300
We can do it with AssistiveTouch.

22
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:55,300
Add a screenshot option
to it - it's very simple.

23
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,020
Go to your Settings,

24
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:59,910
search for AssistiveTouch there,

25
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:02,830
and you'll find the option to turn it on.

26
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,230
Turn it on.

27
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:07,640
Once it's on, AssistiveTouch
shows up like this.

28
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,530
Many people know this much.

29
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:12,550
From here, select
Customise Top Level Menu.

30
00:01:12,930 --> 00:01:16,340
Now you can add the
screenshot option here.

31
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,330
To add it,

32
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:21,380
tap the plus icon at the bottom.

33
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:24,640
After tapping plus, choose Device.

34
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,530
Under Device, pick Screenshot,

35
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:30,160
then tap the check mark at the top.

36
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:32,600
You'll see Screenshot added here.

37
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,710
Now open AssistiveTouch,

38
00:01:35,710 --> 00:01:38,530
and the screenshot option is right there.

39
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:41,020
That's how simply you
can take a screenshot.

40
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,110
Tip two: restart.

41
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:45,550
Normally, to restart our iPhone,

42
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:49,860
we use a Siri shortcut
or the power button.

43
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:53,110
But there's a simpler
way: just like before,

44
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:58,240
in AssistiveTouch, we
can add a restart option.

45
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,780
This one, too, many people know -

46
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,000
but more people don't.

47
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:06,130
The benefit: when your phone hangs,

48
00:02:06,130 --> 00:02:09,340
you can restart it easily.

49
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:12,100
Or any time you want to restart -

50
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:15,280
really simply, without
pressing any button,

51
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,760
right from AssistiveTouch,
wherever it sits on screen,

52
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,320
you can restart your phone.

53
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:23,810
This is an old option too - not new.

54
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,430
To set it up, just like before,

55
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:28,880
go to the AssistiveTouch section,

56
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:32,340
and select Customise Top Level Menu.

57
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,460
As before, tap the plus icon,

58
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:37,700
then tap the plus again.

59
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:40,730
From here, choose System,

60
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:43,220
then select Restart.

61
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,420
Then, as before, enable the check mark.

62
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:50,960
Open AssistiveTouch, and
the restart option is there.

63
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:55,300
So - two really useful, simple tips.

64
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:57,690
To every iPhone user out there - share it,

65
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,760
let them know this is possible.

66
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:03,400
See you again with a new topic!

